 75AS    76SE(D,3HE),(POL D,3HE)       1983RO08,2009KA06,2008KAZT13NDS    201309
 75AS  H TYP=FUL$AUT=ALEXANDRU NEGRET, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 114, 841 (2013)$    
 75AS2 H CUT=30-Jun-2013$                                                       
 75AS c  Includes {+76}Se(pol d,{+3}He)                                         
 75AS c  1983Ro08: (d,{+3}He) E=25.2 MeV. Enriched and natural targets.         
 75AS2c  Magnetic spectrograph; DWBA calculations; FWHM=9-13 keV, measured      
 75AS3c  Q values, |s(|q) at angles between 6|' and 33|'.                       
 75AS c  2009Ka06 (also 2008KaZT): E=80 MeV vector-polarized beam of            
 75AS2c  deuterons with a{-y}=0.520 {i10} provided by the avf                   
 75AS3c  cyclotron at rcnp, Osaka. Enriched target. {+3}He outgoing particles   
 75AS4c  detected and analyzed with Grand Raiden magnetic spectrometer, with    
 75AS5c  an angular aperture of |+1.1|'. FWHM=50 keV                            
 75AS6c  Measured precise absolute cross sections and relative cross sections   
 75AS7c  where these are maximum for the relevant L transfer, angular           
 75AS8c  distributions and polarization asymmetries. Vector analyzing powers    
 75AS9c  were deduced from the measured polarization asymmetries.               
 75ASac  Spectroscopic factors were deduced from analysis of cross              
 75ASbc  section data by DWBA calculations using ptolemy code and six           
 75AScc  different sets of optical-model potential parameters and two           
 75ASdc  bound-state potential parameters. The polarized deuteron beam is also  
 75ASec  used to obtain asymmetries and subsequent information about parities   
 75ASfc  of levels.                                                             
 75ASgc  Uncertainty in cross sections: statistical uncertainty of 1%           
 75AShc  for strong peaks; systematic uncertainties of 5% in absolute values    
 75ASic  and 3% in relative values. Multiplets have larger uncertainties        
 75AS cL E$From 1983Ro08, unless otherwise stated                               
 75AS cL E(X)$265, 280 and 304 groups are unresolved in 2008KaZT,               
 75AS2cL angle-to-angle ratios of cross sections used to assign separate        
 75AS3cL cross sections.                                                        
 75AS cL E(Y)$572 and 585 groups are unresolved in 2008KaZT, angle-to-angle     
 75AS2cL ratios of cross sections used to assign separate cross sections.       
 75AS cL E(Z)$ 1431 group in 2008KaZT corresponds to L=1+4 doublet as in earlier
 75AS2cL literature (although L=1 was also proposed in another study, albeit    
 75AS3cL with a poor fit to angular distribution), angle-to-angle ratios of     
 75AS4cL cross sections used to assign separate cross sections.                 
 75AS cL J(B)$ From measured polarization asymmetry and deduced vector          
 75AS2cL analyzing powers in 2008KaZT.                                          
 75AS CL S$LABEL=C2S                                                            
 75AS cL S$From 2008KaZT if not specified otherwise. The spectroscopic          
 75AS2cL factors were deduced for different L transfers as follows: 4.5|' data  
 75AS3cL for L=1, 8|' data for L=3, and 12|' data for L=4. The values are the   
 75AS4cL ratios of experimental cross sections and calculated DWBA cross        
 75AS5cL sections using the finite-range PTOLEMY code. Six different sets of    
 75AS6cL optical-model potential parameters and two different bound-state       
 75AS7cL potential parameters were used for the calculations. Differences in    
 75AS8cL C{+2}S values were less than 10% for different sets of optical         
 75AS9cL parameters used. The effects of the bound-state parameters were also   
 75ASacL within the uncertainties.                                              
 75ASbcL Authors of 1983Ro08 say that the influence of J on S is only of        
 75ASccL the order of 20%. They also note that S should be multiplied by 1.2    
 75ASdcL if J|p=1/2- rather than 3/2- and by a factor of 1.7 if J|p=5/2-        
 75ASecL rather than 7/2-.                                                      
 75AS cL S(K)$For L+1/2                                                         
 75AS cL S(L)$For L-1/2                                                         
